Design a priority encoder that takes an 8-bit input and outputs a 3-bit representation of the highest priority active bit. The output corresponds to the index of the most significant bit (MSB) that is set to 1, with priorities assigned from highest (bit 7) to lowest (bit 0). If no bits are active, the output will be set to zero.
