description:
Design a circuit that converts a 3-bit selection input into a 2-bit binary output. The module uses a combinational logic structure where the output `bin` corresponds to the binary representation of the lower two bits of the selection `sel`, mapping the 3 possible values of `sel` ranging from 0 to 3, while any other value defaults the output to 00.
module top_module(
    input wire [2:0] sel,
    output reg [1:0] bin
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input wire [2:0] sel,
    output reg [1:0] bin
    );always @ (*) begin
        case (sel)
            3'b000 : bin = 2'b00;
            3'b001 : bin = 2'b01;
            3'b010 : bin = 2'b10;
            3'b011 : bin = 2'b11;
            default : bin = 2'b00;
        endcase
    end
endmodule

